WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.530
(suspenseful music)

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:03.120
- [Narrator] The armed
insurrection launched

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.610
by the chief of the
paramilitary Wagner Group,

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:09.060
Yevgeny Prigozhin, lasted less than a day,

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:10.830
but it was the biggest challenge

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:13.030
to the rule of the Russian president.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:17.550
(Vladimir Putin Speaking foreign language)

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.650
- [Narrator] On Saturday, Wagner seized

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:21.870
the southern military
district headquarters

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:25.080
in the city of Rostov,
the main logistical hub

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.903
for Russian forces operating in Ukraine.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:30.420
They were rolling towards Moscow

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.930
when a deal set to be negotiated
by the Belarusian president

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.390
between Prigozhin and Putin averted

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:38.670
a potential confrontation.

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:41.760
The Wall Street Journal's Moscow
bureau chief, Ann Simmons,

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.823
explains what the short-lived
mutiny means for Putin.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.870
- This crisis is the
most significant test,

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:53.010
I believe, that Putin has
faced in his 23 year rule.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:56.340
Putin had to back down
to a certain degree,

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:59.940
because he had to go to
the negotiating table.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.380
In the morning on Saturday,

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:04.980
we had Vladimir Putin accusing Prigozhin

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:07.650
of instigating an armed rebellion.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:10.860
By the evening, we were
seeing that Prigozhin

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.350
is forgiven and the charge is dropped.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:14.820
Now, we do not know

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:18.300
what kind of deal
Prigozhin got out of this,

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.990
it is said that he will
be going to Belarus,

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:24.450
but the Russian population has now seen

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:27.930
that President Putin isn't as invincible.

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:31.200
This is definitely exposed vulnerability

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:34.530
of his power in the eyes
of the Russian elite.

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:37.680
In terms of what this crisis shows,

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:41.910
it shows that there was
very little resistance

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:44.343
to Prigozhin on his way to Moscow.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.940
The very fact that
Prigozhin and his troops

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:51.090
were able to get within striking distance

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:53.670
of Moscow speaks volumes.

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:56.130
It shows on the one hand that soldiers

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:58.800
in the Russian military
maybe weren't willing

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.440
to take up arms against Prigozhin.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.390
His force is quite feared,

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:07.380
and we also have to note
that a large portion

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:10.980
of Russia's army is now on
the front lines of Ukraine.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.170
Also, there were pictures and videos

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:16.500
of people actually greeting
Prigozhin and his troops,

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:18.690
at least in Rostov in the south,

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:22.320
that shows that maybe there
is this level of support

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:26.163
for Prigozhin that Putin
probably underestimated.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:32.040
The question now will be, how
does vladimir Putin regain

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.837
the narrative that despite
that slight glitch,

00:02:34.837 --> 00:02:37.950
"Nothing has changed, I still have power."

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:40.620
But it's definitely clear that his power,

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:44.793
at least the perception of
his power, has been eroded.

